---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Panel from '../../components/Panel.astro'
import '../../styles/style.css'
---

<Layout title='Home | GRCS' lang="en">
    <Panel margin='4rem 4rem 0rem ' padding='0rem 2rem'>
        <h2>
            New school year registration started, forms are 
            summarized at <a href="/en/registration">this page</a>
        </h2>
    </Panel>
    <Panel margin='2rem 4rem 0rem' padding='1rem 2rem'>
        <h2>
            About us
        </h2>

        <p>
            Grand River Chinese School was established in 2007, it is a non-profit 
            Chinese school serving the greater Kitchener-Waterloo (KW) region, Ontario,
            Canada. Beginning September 2009, most Chinese language courses have been 
            converted to the international language courses managed by the 
            (<a href="https://stlouis.wcdsb.ca/">Waterloo Catholic District School Board</a>), 
            and after that Grand River Chinese 
            School as a non-profit organization continues to contribute to the enrichments and 
            enhancements of the Chinese language programs.
        </p>
        <p>
        Grand River Chinese School offers a series of Chinese language courses for school age 
        children, including CFL (Chinese as a Foreign Language) course for students from non-Chinese 
        family backgrounds, 3-year-old Chinese language course, elementary Chinese language courses
         (JK through Grade 8), secondary Chinese language credit courses (Grades 9 though 12, including 
         a beginnner level credit course). 
        </p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel margin='2rem 4rem 0rem' padding='1rem 2rem'>
        <h2>Schedules</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Classes: 
                    <ul>
                        <li>Main site: Every Saturday</li> 
                        <li>Satellite Site: Every Monday</li>   
                    </ul>
                </strong>
            </li>

            <li>
                First Class: 
                <ul>
                    <li>Main site: September 26, 2025</li> 
                    <li>Satellite Site: September 28, 2026</li>   
                </ul>
            </li>
            
            <li>
                Last Class: 
                <ul>
                    <li>Main site: September 26, 2025</li> 
                    <li>Satellite Site: September 28, 2026</li>   
                </ul>
            </li>

            <li>
                Meet & Greet Day: 
                <ul>
                    <li>Main site: September 19, 2026</li> 
                    <li>Satellite Site: September 21, 2026</li>   
                </ul>
            </li>

            <li>
                No classes:
                <ul>
                    <li>Main site: Oct 10 , Dec 19, Dec 26, 2026, Jan 2, Feb 13, Mar 20 and 27, May 22, 2027</li> 
                    <li>Satellite site: Oct 12 , Dec 21, Dec 28, 2026, Feb 15, Mar 15 and 29, May 24, 2027</li>   
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            
        </p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel margin="2rem 4rem 0rem" padding='1rem 2rem'>
        <h2>Extracurriculars</h2>
        <p>
            In addition to Chinese language programs, the school also provide a series of extracurricular
            interest classes, including:
        </p>
        <h3>Fine Arts</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Children's Art Class</li>
            <li>Watercolour Painting Class</li>
            <li>Sketching Class</li>
            <li>Chinese Ink Painting Class</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Performance Arts</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Chinese Folk Dance Class</li>
            <li>Erhu Class</li>
            <li>Music and Movement Class for Young Children</li>
            <li>Children’s Singing Class</li>
            <li>Vocal Class</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Knowledge</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Programming Class</li>
            <li>Arduino & Programmable Hardware Class</li>
            <li>English Writing</li>
            <li>LEGO Creation Class</li>
            <li>LEGO Robots Class</li>
            <li>Casual Math Class</li>
            <li>Math Enrichment Class</li>
            <li>Olympic Math Class</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Skills</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Chess Class</li>
            <li>"Go" class</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Student Council and multiple student clubs also provide opportunities 
            for students to develop leadership and other skills. 
        </p>
    </Panel>

    <Panel margin="2rem 4rem 0rem" padding='1rem 2rem'>
        <h2>Why Choose Us?</h2>
        <i>
            Excellent teachers, small class learning environments, teaching methodology 
            that combines Chinese tradition and Canadian style, strict safety measures 
            and rich student activities are among the reasons that our school attract 
            more and more students.
        </i>
        <p>
            Elizabeth Witmer, MPP, The Hon. Karen Redman, P.C., M.P., Brenda Halloran, 
            Mayor of Waterloo, and The Hon. Andrew Telegdi, P.C., M.P. sent letters 
            respectively in 2007 to congratulate the establishment of Grand River 
            Chinese School. In 2009, Harold Albrecht, MP also sent letter to our school 
            recognizing the service we've offered to the community.
        </p>
        <p>
            GRCS celebrated 10th anniversary in September 2017. Canadian Prime Minister 
            the Rt. Hon. Justin Trudeau, Consul General He Wei of the People’s Republic 
            of China, MP Hon. Harold Albrecht, MP Hon. Bardish Chagger, MPP Hon. 
            Catherine Fife, MPP Hon. Michael Harris, MPP Hon. Daiene Vernile, 
            Mayor Dave Jaworsky, Mayor Berry Vrbanovic, WCDSB Director of Education Loretta Notten, 
            Principal of St. Louis Cont. Edu. Centres Paul Cox sent greeting letters, respectively, 
            to the GRCS Journal.
        </p>
    </Panel>
</Layout>

<style>
